'''Tatewaki Kuno (Gi)''' is a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Ranma 1/2 Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 10.4 Update|Version 10.4]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 603
|rarity = SR
|name1 = Tatewaki Kuno (Gi)
|name2 = Tatewaki Kuno
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Tatewaki Kuno''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Tatewaki has good slow chance with multi-hit, but unfortunately not 100% uptime. It is still decent, though. His knockback ability, however, is very situational. Sometimes, when there is no backliner, it can be quite beneficial, however Angel enemies usually appear with some sort of backliner or midranger, where the knockback ability can hinder your chances to beat the stage. In these situations, Tatewaki's dodge can kick in and save him, but this requires a lot of luck to pull off. For the same reason, the dodge ability should not be relied on and treated as a bonus. Even if Tatewaki does not die, your stack will.

Tatewaki Kuno is best described as unit similar to [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]] in terms of generalist usage, with [[:Category:Angel Enemies|anti-angel]] crowd controlling abilities. However, while Tatewaki has higher health and DPS. On the other hand, Surfer has faster cooldown, more knockbacks, lower cost and the [[Survive]] ability, meaning it is recommended to use Surfer Cat over him.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Midranger}}

